    "Psa",
    "Psm"
  ],
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "verse-001",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 1,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:144:1",
      "numberLabel": "1",
      "text": "Blessed be the LORD my strength, which teacheth my hands to war, and my fingers to fight:",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 144:1",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:144:1"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-002",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 2,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:144:2",
      "numberLabel": "2",
      "text": "My goodness, and my fortress; my high tower, and my deliverer; my shield, and he in whom I trust; who subdueth my people under me.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 144:2",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:144:2"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-003",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 3,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:144:3",
      "numberLabel": "3",
      "text": "LORD, what is man, that thou takest knowledge of him! or the son of man, that thou makest account of him!",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 144:3",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:144:3"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-004",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 4,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:144:4",
      "numberLabel": "4",
      "text": "Man is like to vanity: his days are as a shadow that passeth away.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 144:4",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:144:4"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-005",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 5,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:144:5",
      "numberLabel": "5",
      "text": "Bow thy heavens, O LORD, and come down: touch the mountains, and they shall smoke.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 144:5",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:144:5"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-006",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 6,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:144:6",
      "numberLabel": "6",
      "text": "Cast forth lightning, and scatter them: shoot out thine arrows, and destroy them.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 144:6",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:144:6"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-007",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 7,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:144:7",
      "numberLabel": "7",
      "text": "Send thine hand from above; rid me, and deliver me out of great waters, from the hand of strange children;",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 144:7",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:144:7"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-008",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 8,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:144:8",
      "numberLabel": "8",
      "text": "Whose mouth speaketh vanity, and their right hand is a right hand of falsehood.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 144:8",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:144:8"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-009",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 9,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:144:9",
      "numberLabel": "9",
      "text": "I will sing a new song unto thee, O God: upon a psaltery and an instrument of ten strings will I sing praises unto thee.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 144:9",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:144:9"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-010",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 10,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:144:10",
      "numberLabel": "10",
      "text": "It is he that giveth salvation unto kings: who delivereth David his servant from the hurtful sword.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 144:10",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:144:10"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-011",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 11,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:144:11",
      "numberLabel": "11",
      "text": "Rid me, and deliver me from the hand of strange children, whose mouth speaketh vanity, and their right hand is a right hand of falsehood:",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 144:11",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:144:11"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-012",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 12,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:144:12",
      "numberLabel": "12",
      "text": "That our sons may be as plants grown up in their youth; that our daughters may be as corner stones, polished after the similitude of a palace:",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 144:12",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:144:12"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-013",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 13,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:144:13",
      "numberLabel": "13",
      "text": "That our garners may be full, affording all manner of store: that our sheep may bring forth thousands and ten thousands in our streets:",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 144:13",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:144:13"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-014",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 14,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:144:14",
      "numberLabel": "14",
      "text": "That our oxen may be strong to labour; that there be no breaking in, nor going out; that there be no complaining in our streets.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 144:14",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:144:14"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-015",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 15,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:144:15",
      "numberLabel": "15",
      "text": "Happy is that people, that is in such a case: yea, happy is that people, whose God is the LORD.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 144:15",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:144:15"
      }
    }
  ],
  "source": {
